  "ce:2014:ga:q8-s2": {
    concept: "Quantitative Aptitude - Ratio of Revenue per Unit Quantity",
    markdown: "From the two pie charts (total quantity $5$ lakh tonnes, total revenue $250$ crore rupees):\n\n- Item 1: $20\\%$ of quantity, $40\\%$ of revenue.\n- Item 4: $40\\%$ of quantity, $20\\%$ of revenue.\n\nRevenue per kg for an item is proportional to $(\\text{revenue }\\%)/(\\text{quantity }\\%)$:\n\n$$\\frac{R_1/Q_1}{R_4/Q_4} = \\frac{40/20}{20/40} = \\frac{2}{0.5} = 4.$$\n\nThus the ratio is $4:1$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is **Option D (04:01)**.",
    images: ["/question-images/ce/2014/ce-2014-a8649f3246.webp"]
  },

  "ce:2014:ga:q9-s2": {
    concept: "Quantitative Aptitude - Coordinate Geometry (Compass Directions)",
    markdown: "Take $Z=(0,0)$ with east as $+x$ and north as $+y$. Use unit vectors at $45^\\circ$ for NE/SE.\n\n- $Y$ is $1$ km SE of $Z$: $Y=(\\frac1{\\sqrt2},-\\frac1{\\sqrt2})$.\n- $X$ is $1$ km NE of $Y$: $X=Y+(\\frac1{\\sqrt2},\\frac1{\\sqrt2})=(\\sqrt2,0)$.\n- $W$ is $1$ km west of $Z$: $W=(-1,0)$.\n- $P$ is $1$ km south of $W$: $P=(-1,-1)$.\n- $Q$ is $1$ km east of $P$: $Q=(0,-1)$.\n\nDistance $XQ$:\n\n$$\\sqrt{(\\sqrt2-0)^2+(0-(-1))^2}=\\sqrt{2+1}=\\sqrt3.$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is **Option C ($\\sqrt{3}$)**.",
    images: []
  },

  "ce:2014:ga:q10-s2": {
    concept: "Quantitative Aptitude - Bayes' Theorem (Diagnostic Testing)",
    markdown: "Let $H$ = actually HIV$^+$. $P(H)=0.10$, $P(H^c)=0.90$.\nSensitivity $P(T^+|H)=0.95$; false-positive rate $P(T^+|H^c)=1-0.89=0.11$.\n\nBy Bayes' theorem:\n\n$$P(H|T^+) = \\frac{P(T^+|H)P(H)}{P(T^+|H)P(H)+P(T^+|H^c)P(H^c)}\n= \\frac{0.95\\times0.10}{0.95\\times0.10+0.11\\times0.90}\n= \\frac{0.095}{0.095+0.099}\n= \\frac{0.095}{0.194}\\approx 0.4897.$$\n\nThis is consistent with the official key value $0.485$ (rounded).",
    images: []
  },

